+
+**Formulas:**
+For a sphere intersection, the ray $\mathbf{P}(t) = \mathbf{O} + t\mathbf{D}$ intersects the sphere when:
+$$a = \mathbf{D} \cdot \mathbf{D}$$
+$$\mathbf{oc} = \mathbf{O} - C$$
+$$b = 2(\mathbf{oc} \cdot \mathbf{D})$$
+$$c = \mathbf{oc} \cdot \mathbf{oc} - R^2$$
+$$\Delta = b^2 - 4ac$$
+$$t_{enter} = \frac{-b - \sqrt{\Delta}}{2a}, \quad t_{exit} = \frac{-b + \sqrt{\Delta}}{2a}$$
+where $t_{enter}$ and $t_{exit}$ are the distances along the ray to the entry and exit points, respectively [G].
 
